WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.240
The DC rumor mill has cranked out a real doozy.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:07.600
According to the rumor mongers at We Got This
Covered, Warner Bros. and DC Films have eyes

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.040
on a big name to portray the next version
of the Joker, who will face off against Robert

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.960
Pattinson's Batman: Johnny Depp.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.200
"I've been considering things that begin with
the letter M. 'Moron.'

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.060
'Mutiny.'

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.360
'Murder.'

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.840
It seems unlikely that the Clown Prince of
Crime will pop up in writer-director Matt

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.949
Reeves' upcoming The Batman, in which Pattinson's
Dark Knight will make his debut.

00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:33.860
We Got This Covered's supposed sources don't
dispute that.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.320
Instead, they're alleging that Warner Bros.
is already looking to lock down the Joker

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:41.469
role for a sequel to Battinson's first outing,
and that Depp is at the top of their list

00:00:41.469 --> 00:00:42.140
of candidates.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.040
If we're being honest, that feels pretty unlikely
too.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.680
As you may be aware, WGTC is not exactly a
super-reliable source of inside information.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:54.640
No other media outlets have even caught a
whiff of this potential casting, and Depp

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.960
is currently under, shall we say, a little
bit of scrutiny in the media.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.200
This all adds up to this rumor most likely
being, as they say, a bunch of hooey.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.220
That doesn't mean that Pattinson's Bruce Wayne
won't have to contend with his cackling arch-nemesis

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:07.260
at some point, however.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:11.220
In fact, we find it quite likely that The
Batman's inevitable sequel could introduce

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:11.860
the Joker.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:15.580
Absent some more reputable sources, though,
we just don't think it'll be Johnny Depp in

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.080
the role.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:20.220
Assuming that The Batman does get at least
one follow-up picture, it seems silly to think

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.320
that the Joker won't get involved at some
point.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.940
There's one thing, however, that we know for
sure and if we've said this once, we've said

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.080
this a million times.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:31.080
But, just in case you forgot, here's one last
reminder: It won't be the version portrayed

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.820
by Joaquin Phoenix in last year's billion-dollar
hit Joker.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.920
"I'm-a just trying to make people laugh."

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:37.820
"And how's that going for ya?"

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.300
We know this for more than one reason, not
the least of which is that Joker's director,

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:51.090
Todd Phillips, shot any speculation on the
matter full of holes long before the flick

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.180
was even released.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:56.140
Variety reports that, when asked about the
possibility of Phoenix's Arthur Fleck having

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:00.570
a run-in with Pattinson's Caped Crusader at
some point, Phillips flatly stated, quote,

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:01.900
"No, definitely not.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.580
There will be many more Jokers, I'm sure,
in the future."

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.720
Since then, we've gotten photos from the set
of The Batman which strongly indicate that

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.420
the picture is set no earlier than the mid-2000s.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.560
Considering that Joker was set in 1981, this
would mean that Arthur Fleck would be just

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:20.069
a bit too old to take on the young, sprightly
Batman who will be featured in Reeves' movies.

00:02:20.069 --> 00:02:24.180
For that matter, the 56-year-old Depp is also
probably a bit too long in the tooth to be

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:28.660
seriously considered for the role of the Joker
to say nothing of fan-favorite choice Willem

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.110
Dafoe, who is even older.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.239
No, the next actor to step into the Joker's
clown shoes is likely to be much closer in

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.310
age to the 33-year-old Pattinson.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:40.560
Anyway, speaking of Joker… while Joker 2
hasn't yet been confirmed, it seems all but

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.640
inevitable given the first movie's stellar
box office performance.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:48.020
If it happens to get the green light sooner
rather than later, then there's a chance that

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:52.500
Arthur Fleck's next big-screen appearance
could arrive before O Batman, Where Art Thou…

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:55.019
or whatever The Batman's sequel actually ends
up being called.

00:02:55.019 --> 00:02:59.150
If this is the case, then our next cinematic
Joker could be part of a two-fer as the rumor

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:03.590
mill has also recently suggested that Joker
2 will see Arthur contending with the real

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:07.600
Joker, a younger, even more violent criminal
who was influenced by the events of the first

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:08.100
film.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:13.120
The Rumor-O-Matic has even spit out one possibility
as to who might take on the role: Ben Barnes,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.200
who portrayed Jigsaw in the Marvel Netflix
series The Punisher.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:20.739
Of course, until we hear something official,
we're inclined to file this under "W.S." for

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:23.980
"Wild Speculation" or even "B.S.," for you
know what.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.890
The big Bat-picture will undoubtedly become
clearer when The Batman hits the big screen

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:30.160
on June 25, 2021.

